@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## Features
+
+### JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to. It throws a
+`SyntaxError` when the pointer is not valid (it must be empty or start with `/`, and `~` must be
+followed by `0` or `1`), and a `RangeError` when it does not resolve: missing member, array index out
+of range or not canonical (`01`, `-1`), the `-` token (a nonexistent element), or descending into a
+primitive. Only own members are resolved, so `/toString` or `/__proto__` never reach inherited values.
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
